  "answer": "Implemented `paginate` in `pagination.mjs`. Summary of the changes:\n\n**Validation**\n- `items` non-array → `TypeError`.\n- `page` / `pageSize` not positive safe integers → `RangeError` (uses `Number.isSafeInteger`, which also rejects `NaN`, `Infinity`, floats, and non-numbers).\n\n**Behavior**\n- 1-based paging: `start = (page - 1) * pageSize`.\n- `items` is a fresh array via `slice` (original order preserved, input and elements untouched).\n- `totalPages = Math.ceil(items.length / pageSize)` — empty input yields `0`.\n- `nextPage = page < totalPages ? page + 1 : null`, so it's `null` on the last page, for empty input, and for any page beyond the last (while `totalPages` still reflects the real count).\n- Named export `paginate` retained.\n\nThe original had three bugs, all fixed: it used `page * pageSize` (off-by-one, treating page 1 as the second page), `Math.floor` instead of `Math.ceil` for `totalPages`, and always returned `page + 1` for `nextPage` with no bounds check or validation.",
